# Return the arm to its home posture: a joint-space move of the six arm
# joints to the configured `home_joints` target (default all-zeros, the JAKA
# reference posture). The gripper is NOT commanded — anything held stays
# held (use `release` first to let go).
#
# Request has no fields — the tool takes no arguments ({}).
---
# Whether the arm reached the home posture (every joint within tolerance).
bool success

# Human-readable status. On failure, names the failing stage
# (preflight / home/move).
string message

# How long the whole call took (s).
float32 elapsed_s
